ISO/IEC 29100
-------------

src/iso29100/schema/*.yaml, src/iso29100/datamodel/ and project/ model the
records an organization keeps when it applies the privacy framework of
ISO/IEC 29100:2024, Information technology - Security techniques - Privacy
framework (second edition, 2024-02). They are this project's own work, and
they are not endorsed by ISO or IEC.

The standard's text is copyright ISO and IEC. This repository carries none of
it: no clause or heading, copied or paraphrased sentence by sentence. Each
title and description is this project's own, written to say what an element is
for. Copyright protects how the standard is expressed, not the methods and
facts it describes. The project nevertheless takes the stricter reading that
European law allows after Infopaq (C-5/08), under which even a short extract
can be protected when it shows its author's own choices, so it reuses no
heading or phrase of the standard. The terms the standard defines and the
privacy field shares, such as PII principal, are used as names. The standard
remains the authority on what it says, and this project's words do not replace
it.

This repository's licence grants no right to reproduce or redistribute that
text. Obtain the standard and any licence to reuse its text from ISO or your
national standards body. A title or description slot holds whatever its user
writes: fill it only with text you have the right to use.

Some elements cite the subclause they model by number, so a reader with a
licensed copy can look the text up there. The numbers come from a third party's
public outline of the edition, not from the standard. ISO's Customer Licence
Agreement also restricts use of the text with AI tools, so the standard is never
given to the agents that maintain this repository's knowledge bundle.
scripts/check_overlap.py lets a licence holder test this repository's words and
numbers against their own copy, which stays outside the repository.

ISO Open Data
-------------

src/iso29100/schema/iso-open-data/iso_deliverables_metadata.jsonl holds ISO's
records of ISO/IEC 29100:2024, ISO/IEC 29100:2011 and ISO/IEC
29100:2011/Amd 1:2018, taken on 2026-11-05 from
https://isopublicstorageprod.blob.core.windows.net/opendata/_latest/iso_deliverables_metadata/json/iso_deliverables_metadata.jsonl.
Each line is ISO's record as published, without its "scope" field.
scripts/check_upstream_release.py pins each line by its hash and compares it
with the live dataset.

